    "samples": "Each run warms up 30 frames then records 180 consecutive successful frames. Each physical presentation window has its own sample count. Four paired process restarts per arm. Time summaries use the median of the four run p95s.",
    "bridge": "The probe reads the byte length submitted to native. Geometry bytes include vertex/index payload plus the 12-byte definition header for each mesh. Every frame still carries all draw, material, camera and HUD data.",
    "timing": "copyUs is V8-to-Java buffer copying. dispatchToEnqueueUs ends at the UI thread enqueue. nativeDrawUs brackets the JNI draw call through its return and includes GLES submission CPU time. submittedIntervalUs is time between UI callbacks on successful submissions. presentUs uses actual presentation timestamps on the SurfaceFlinger game buffer layer.",
    "memory": "residentPayloadBytes is the sum of live vertex/index payloads in one native CPU copy. The GLES buffers have the same logical payload. This excludes textures, driver allocation overhead and VM memory. processPssKiB is one process-wide reading per run after timing.",
    "refresh": "The app requested 60 Hz. At the start of the first baseline window the compositor reported an 8.33 ms refresh period, and 16.67 ms in the remaining seven. The game layer presented close to 60 Hz throughout."
